        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The recommendation for using <a href=\"https://github.com/fregante/browser-extension-template\">browser-extension-template</a> to set up an extension project was removed from the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/Build_a_cross_browser_extension\" rel=\"nofollow\">Build a cross-browser extension</a> page in October 2022. At that time, the template was updated to Manifest V3, but the how-to page has not been updated.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The how-to page has been updated to cover Manifest V3, so the recommendation can be restored.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes #121826</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43777",
            "title": "Issue 21826: Restore browser-extension-template recommendation",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T00:06:25.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-14T00:04:47.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62723358?u=f3632393d0193c912fa572def786f97a3e49c40b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/style-src-attr#violation_cases\" rel=\"nofollow\">Content-Security-Policy: style-src-attr directive &gt; Examples &gt; Violation cases</a>, change the style attribute value to something that does not use a keyword.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I intend to avoid possible confusion. A user might think <code class=\"notranslate\">style-src-attr 'none'</code> blocks <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;div style=\"display:none\"&gt;Foo&lt;/div&gt;</code> because it has \"none\" in the attribute value. (At least one user was confused… me.)</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>",
