        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome has added support for two features that allow sites to size fonts in proportion to the operating system/browser text scale settings:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;meta name=\"text-scale\" content=\"...\" /&gt;</code> element, which was added in Chrome 146, and works across Desktop and Mobile platforms. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5112244702674944\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5112244702674944</a>.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">preferred-text-scale</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">env()</code> variable, which was added in Chrome 138. This only really works in Android,</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR documents both of these features.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43766",
            "title": "Technical review: Document meta text-scale and env(preferred-text-scale)",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-15T08:53:07.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T13:09:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF150 adds support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/script/type/importmap#merging_multiple_import_maps\" rel=\"nofollow\">multiple import maps</a> behind a pref (<code class=\"notranslate\">dom.multiple_import_maps.enabled</code>). This adds an experimental feature and release note entry.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It also adds a minor clarification to the JS doc.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4127672727\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43551\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43551/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43551\">#43551</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43759",
            "title": "FF150 Expr Feature - multiple JS import maps",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-13T23:17:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T07:06:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118266?u=5a7fb2f3d1ecc7dcd73f43f4b478cb4938e6572c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds docs for the <code class=\"notranslate\">shadowrootslotassignment</code> attribute.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Trying to add the docs so that <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4083478419\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12267\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/12267/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12267\">whatwg/html#12267</a> can be merged.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've largely cribbed the docs style from the other <code class=\"notranslate\">shadowroot*</code> attributes.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4247549777\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29457\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29457/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29457\">mdn/browser-compat-data#29457</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43753",
            "title": "Add shadowrootslotassignment attribute",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T09:28:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-12T09:38:53.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "keithamus",
                "url": "https://github.com/keithamus"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88993368?u=3e60c7d167b03a8cb435e71361ac5708dee39416&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The pseudo element ::-webkit-inner-spin-button page property has a reference link below the See also section:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>[Styling Form Controls – WebKit</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As part of Apple's restructuring documentation, this link doesn't work anymore and is returning a 504 server error.<br>\nI propose removing it from the page.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clean up the documentation and avoid reference confusion.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">(<a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/::-webkit-inner-spin-button\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/::-webkit-inner-spin-button</a>)</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43750",
            "title": "Remove 504'ed WebKit Trac link",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T22:41:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-11T21:56:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Buenaventura0",
                "url": "https://github.com/Buenaventura0"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137640490?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Added a note section that describes that sibling combinators to the right of :scope never match.<br>\nExplicit examples showing :scope + * and :scope ~ * as selectors that never match with firefox generated warnings.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">It updates the documentation and makes the reader to understand proper working of scope without bugs.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n <span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42364.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3722993694\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42364\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42364/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42364\">#42364</a>\n\n\n",
